# Elementor Build Standards

## Layout

Use Elementor Flexbox Containers.

Do not use legacy Sections or Columns.

Prefer a shallow and understandable DOM structure.

Do not create unnecessary nested containers.

Every major visual section should have its own top-level container.

## Global design system

Always prefer Elementor Global Colors and Global Typography.

Never repeatedly hard-code a color or typography value when a corresponding global token exists.

Before building pages, read:

@specifications/design-system.md
@specifications/components.md

Use these specifications as the implementation source of truth.

## Containers

Use consistent content widths from the design system.

Use responsive padding and gap settings.

Do not compensate for incorrect structure using arbitrary margins.

Prefer:
- container gap
- padding
- flex alignment

over negative margins.

## Typography

Use global typography styles whenever possible.

Respect:
- font family
- weight
- line height
- letter spacing
- responsive font sizes

from the approved design system.

## Components

Reuse visual patterns.

Examples:
- buttons
- product cards
- badges
- USP items
- headings
- icon/text combinations
- CTA blocks

Do not independently redesign the same component on different pages.

## Widgets

Prefer native widgets.

Before using an unfamiliar widget, inspect its schema through EMCP.

Do not emulate an existing Elementor widget with an HTML widget.

## Responsive

Every implementation must be checked at:

Desktop
Tablet
Mobile

Use Elementor responsive overrides rather than creating duplicate sections purely for different viewport sizes unless the design fundamentally requires different markup.

## Images

Maintain the aspect ratio defined by the design.

Do not stretch source images.

Use WordPress Media Library assets.

Always provide appropriate alt text when meaningful.

## WooCommerce

Use WooCommerce and Elementor Pro dynamic widgets for dynamic commerce content.

Do not hard-code:
- product names
- product prices
- product images
- stock state
- add-to-cart URLs

inside product templates when dynamic data is available.